    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d106">

                <pb facs="0221" n="121" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg121"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">360F.1163 Church of Jesus Christ/5:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Czechoslovakia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Benton</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Prague</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-10-11T16:00:00+01:00">October 11, 1934—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 11—2:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>49. Under Secretary of Foreign Office assures me that the information contained
                    in your No. 36, October 8, 4 p.m., will be brought to immediate attention of the
                    competent judge. Arthur Gaillardth [<hi rendition="#italic">Gaeth</hi>] believes
                    it unnecessary to request postponement of the case which is now set for October
                    16th.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Benton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
